llowed Iran  to use it as an excuse to get back out  of the box  when the deal was in force Iran was  making good on its commitments that's  not just me saying it it's independent  International experts in fact it's the  state department under the previous  administration  um when the deal was enforced Iran's  breakout time that is the time it would  be required for it to produce enough  fissile material for one nuclear weapon  had been pushed Beyond one year now it's  a matter of weeks so in and of itself  that's a very unfortunate development  having said that I think the world's  Focus right now is very much on the the  protests that are going on in Iran ever  since the killing of um what do they  tell you about the the stability of the  government right now well I think what  they tell us is this  um  they tell us that the Iranian people  want to be able to speak up and speak  out about the issues that they care  about  they tell us that the regime is afraid  to let that happen and is repressing  their efforts to do just that to be able  to say  um where they want the country to go to  be able to say what they what they want  to wear  and that to me is a sign of a weakness  not strength having said that I'm not  going to make any predictions about  where this goes you know we haven't had  diplomatic relations with Iran for a  long time our own visibility and  understanding of uh the uh the country  of the society is  um as a result uh less than it might be  but fundamentally this is about the  Iranian people it's not about us one of  the big mistakes that the regime makes  is when it sees protests is saying  whether it believes it or not that  they're being instigated by the United  States by some outside power that's a  profound misunderstanding of their own  people and their own country so the  question now is to what extent the  regime responds to the uh the needs the  aspirations the desires of their own  people  okay secretary blanket everybody I'm  afraid 